# calmoji v@VERSION@ — calendar files

Ready-made `.ics` calendar layers from
[calmoji](https://github.com/propertools/Calmoji-Forge), for **@YEARS@**,
in two alignments:

* `academic`: each year runs September → August
* `calendar`: each year runs January → December

Pick one alignment and stick with it.

---

## What's in each year's folder

```
<year>/<alignment>/
├── semester_phases_<year>.ics          ← the seasons of your year (all-day markers)
├── meeting_all_<year>.ics              ← every meeting slot for the year
├── meeting_<phase>_<from>_to_<to>.ics  ← the same slots, one file per phase
├── focus_all_<year>.ics                ← every focus block for the year
├── focus_<phase>_<from>_to_<to>.ics    ← the same blocks, one file per phase
└── ebi48_layer_<year>.ics              ← the EBI48 emoji clock
```

Use **either** `meeting_all` **or** the per-phase meeting files, not both.
Likewise use **either** `focus_all` **or** the per-phase focus files, not
both.

---

## Importing

Import each layer into **its own calendar** (for example "🧠 Focus
Blocks", "🕒 Meeting Slots"), so you can colour it and switch it on and
off on its own. The calmoji
[playbook](https://github.com/propertools/Calmoji-Forge/blob/main/docs/PLAYBOOK.md)
explains how to use the layers day to day.

* **Apple Calendar:** File → Import → choose the file → choose the
  calendar.
* **Google Calendar:** Settings → Import & export → choose the file and
  the destination calendar.
* **Outlook, Fastmail, Thunderbird and others:** use your app's "Import"
  option.

**Focus blocks come one file per phase.** Start with the phase you're in
rather than the whole year; it's a gentler start anyway. Each phase file
holds only that phase's own days, so the files never overlap. If you'd
rather have everything at once, import `focus_all_<year>.ics` instead
(and none of the per-phase files).

To refresh a layer later, delete that calendar, recreate it, and import
again. Your own events, in your own calendars, are untouched.

---

## Known limitations in v@VERSION@

* **Meeting slot labels assume summer time.** Times are correct in UTC,
  but the local-time labels (CEST, EDT, PDT) are an hour off in winter
  for Brussels, Havana and Seattle.
* **The EBI48 clock appears one day a week**, and each entry shows its
  emoji twice.
* **Leap years:** the last day of a leap year (for example 31 August 2028
  in `academic`, 31 December 2028 in `calendar`) belongs to no year's
  files.

All of these are planned for v0.2. See the
[roadmap](https://github.com/propertools/Calmoji-Forge#-roadmap).

---

## Verifying the files

`MANIFEST.sha256` lists the SHA-256 hash of every `.ics` file. From
inside this folder:

```bash
shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256
```

(On Linux, `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256` works too.) Every line should
end in `OK`.

You can also regenerate any year yourself and compare. The output is
byte-identical:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/propertools/Calmoji-Forge.git
cd Calmoji-Forge
git checkout v@VERSION@
python3 calmoji.py --year=2027 --calendar-alignment=academic --output-dir=check
diff -r check /path/to/this/folder/2027/academic
```

